<server>
    siteName := "Dreego"
</server>

<body lang="md">
# Markdown in the Body

The v0.3 md processor lets a {{ siteName }} page body be written as real Markdown. Set `lang="md"` on the body section and the processor converts it to HTML at generation time.

## How it works

A body section with `lang="md"` is parsed by a hand-written, stdlib-only Markdown parser. The result is ordinary HTML, so the rest of the pipeline stays unchanged.

- No external dependencies
- Dreego constructs stay intact
- Output remains close to plain Go and net/http

## What stays protected

Expressions, conditions, and components inside a Markdown body are preserved. You can mix prose with Dreego logic without escaping.

## Keep reading

Back to the [blog index](/blog/), or see the [render foundation](/blog/posts/rendering-foundation) post for the v0.2 story.
</body>
